      "writtenOn": "2026-06-03T21:22:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "the legacy avx2 code actually calls the ssse3 code for w \u003d\u003d 16:\n\nhttps://aomedia.googlesource.com/aom/+/refs/heads/main/aom_dsp/x86/aom_subpixel_8t_intrin_avx2.c#1408\n\nThe ssse3 code uses even/odd split method to further optimize for w\u003d\u003d16 blocks, which is different from how it is done for other block sizes (also different from how highway is)\n\nThere\u0027s less than 1% speed up for overall encoding (two pass good on 720p). I\u0027m not sure if that\u0027s just noise...",
      "parentUuid": "a4f28936_92fd1922",
      "revId": "4d7f0a8e36c9f6e7451f87eb13cf30cb049b56f7",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
